# counter harness. One call is one full-dataset loss and gradient.
# An L-BFGS-B line-search request and an LM error retry each count.
# A repeated weight vector is cached and is not counted again.
# Success requires every parameter-tensor gradient L2 at or below the stop, with the call count under the cap.
# pyamff 8037eb98 stopped on the max absolute entry of each tensor. This row uses the L2 test.
# There is no weight-space Hessian, so wrong_stationary is unused.
# mean_epoch is the half-even mean of the successful call counts.
# RMSE means are arithmetic means of the successes. force_rmse is -1 when the force coefficient is 0.
# Behler-Parrinello squared-error loss on the problem trajectory. Fingerprints come from the archived fpParas.dat. The network has hidden layers 10 and 7, tanh, and a linear output, with NoScaler. Each start is uniform[-1, 1) from PCG64(20261015 + index). One harness call is one full-dataset loss and gradient. The stop is the L2 norm of each parameter-tensor gradient. pyamff 8037eb98 used the max absolute entry. Adam uses mu 0.01, b1 0.9, b2 0.999, and eps 1e-8. The step divides the full-dataset gradient by the structure count. The energy coefficient is 1 and the force coefficient is 0.1. The stop is 0.1 and the cap is 30000.
